          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 425.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "0.06 mm for every spacer. The largest error is for the thick",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 437.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stock, where the crease allowance grows with the number",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 449.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "of layers: the outer layers must bend around a thicker core,",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 461.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "and the crease opens slightly. For the thin and medium",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 473
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stocks the error does not grow with the number of layers,",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 485
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "which agrees with the note of Glue Pot Corner (2022) on",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 496.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "thin paper joints.",
          "width" : 67.2,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 508.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Repeated readings of the same spacer differed by at most",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 526.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "0.02 mm. Spacers that were left in the slot overnight lost",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 538.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "about 0.01 mm of height, which is smaller than the spread",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 550.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "between readings and was ignored.",
          "width" : 139.7,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 562.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "4. Conclusion",
          "width" : 69.1,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 589.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer can be designed from the card thick-",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 610.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ness and a crease allowance measured once for each stock.",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 622.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "For heights up to 2 mm the thin and medium stocks fol-",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 634.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "low the layer model closely, and they are the better choice",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 646.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "when a rail must sit at an exact height. The thick stock",
          "width" : 234,
          "x" : 55.4,
          "y" : 658.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "is quicker to fold but should be checked in the slot when",
